SHANNON ENTROPY CORRECTION LOG
================================================================================
Applied to non-amino acid residues only

METHOD:
-------
Corrects for bias when charge states have different numbers of conformers.
Conformers are grouped by their NUMERIC CHARGE VALUE (e.g., all neutral
states with charge=0 are in one group, regardless of state designation).
Charge states with more conformers are penalized using Shannon entropy
to account for the entropic cost of the conformational distribution.

PROCEDURE:
1. Group conformers by NUMERIC charge value (e.g., charge=0, charge=-1)
2. Convert probabilities to free energies: ΔG/RT = -ln(P_i/P_ref)
3. Normalize probabilities within each charge group
4. Calculate Shannon entropy for each group: E_TS/RT = -Σ(P_i * ln(P_i))
5. Add entropy penalty: ΔG_corrected/RT = ΔG_original/RT + E_TS/RT
6. Convert back to probabilities: P_i = exp(-ΔG_corrected/RT) / Z

CONSTANTS:
R = 0.001987 kcal·K⁻¹·mol⁻¹
T = 298.0 K
RT = 0.592 kcal/mol

PENALTIES (Shannon entropy):
N=1: Entropy = 0.000 → No penalty (0.000 kcal/mol)
N=2 (equal probs): Entropy = 0.693 → Penalty = 0.410 kcal/mol
N=3 (equal probs): Entropy = 1.099 → Penalty = 0.651 kcal/mol
N=4 (equal probs): Entropy = 1.386 → Penalty = 0.821 kcal/mol
Note: Actual penalties depend on the probability distribution within each group

Amino acids excluded from correction:
ACE, ALA, ARG, ASN, ASP, CTG, CTR, CYD, CYS, GLN, GLU, HIS, ILE, LEU, LYS, MET, NME, NTG, NTR, PHE, PRO, SER, THR, TRP, TYR, VAL

